From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:25:22 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 12/32] spiFlash: Macronix factory ESN, and say why there is
 none

Macronix has no unique ID command: a 128-bit ESN is only programmed in
the secured OTP (0x00-0x0F) on "special order", and security register
bit 0 then reads 1 (Macronix AN0218). Read the security register
(RDSCUR 0x2B, a plain read); when factory locked, read the ESN between
ENSO (0xB1) and EXSO (0xC1), always leaving the secured OTP mode.
Otherwise report why there is no unique ID, with the register value,
instead of "unsupported" (new unique_id.note JSON field).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F2L6L5SJYvbBUUt4DinjGC
